.TH TESLAMATE\-RS 1 "2026-09-21" "teslamate-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teslamate\-rs \- single-process TeslaMate with SQLite and built-in dashboards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teslamate\-rs
.RI [ \fB\-\-db\fR " " \fIPATH\fR ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teslamate\-rs
is a RAM-saving rewrite of TeslaMate as a single Rust binary. It stores
data in SQLite rather than PostgreSQL and serves Grafana-parity dashboards
from its own HTTP server, so neither PostgreSQL nor Grafana is needed.
.PP
On Debian the daemon normally runs under systemd as
.BR teslamate\-rs.service ,
which invokes
.B teslamate\-rs serve
and is configured through
.IR /etc/default/teslamate\-rs .
See
.BR README.Debian .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
SQLite database path. Defaults to the packaged service location,
.IR /srv/teslamate\-rs/teslamate\-rs.sqlite .
Also settable with
.BR TESLAMATE_RS_DB .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Serve the dashboards, and start the Tesla Owner API logger if tokens have
been stored. Options:
.BI \-\-bind " ADDR"
(default 127.0.0.1),
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
(default 4010),
.B \-\-no\-logger
to serve without polling Tesla, and
.BI \-\-auth " BACKEND"
where
.I BACKEND
is
.B local
(argon2 hashes in SQLite) or
.B pam
(Linux accounts). The default is
.B pam
when
.I /etc/pam.d/teslamate\-rs
exists, otherwise
.BR local .
.TP
.B login \-\-refresh\-token \fITOKEN\fR
Store an Owner API refresh token and register the vehicles on the account.
.TP
.B import
Import a live TeslaMate PostgreSQL instance through
.BR "docker exec" .
Options:
.BI \-\-docker " CONTAINER"
(default teslamate\-database\-1),
.BI \-\-user " USER"
and
.BI \-\-dbname " NAME"
(both default teslamate).
.TP
.B import\-tokens
Import Cloak-encrypted Owner API tokens from a live TeslaMate instance. Takes
the same options as
.BR import ,
plus
.BI \-\-app " CONTAINER"
(default teslamate\-teslamate\-1).
.TP
.B refresh
Perform a TeslaMate-style Owner API read sweep. Does not send
.BR wake_up ;
vehicle data is fetched only for vehicles already online.
.TP
.B sync\-invoices
Pull Tesla Supercharger invoices through the account API. This does not wake
the car. With
.B \-\-full
it forces an OAuth refresh, lists vehicles, and walks every history page.
.TP
.B seed
Load synthetic drives, charges and positions. No Tesla account is needed.
.TP
.B demo
Seed mock history, run a local Tesla API mock, log in against it, and serve
the dashboards. Options:
.BI \-\-bind " ADDR"
(default 127.0.0.1),
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
(default 4010) and
.BI \-\-mock\-port " PORT"
(default 4070).
.TP
.B probe
Contact Tesla auth, products and vehicle_data as a connectivity check. No
token values are printed.
.TP
.B doctor
Print the schema and per-table row counts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every option below can also be set in
.IR /etc/default/teslamate\-rs .
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_DB
SQLite database path.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_HOME
Service data directory.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_BIND
.TQ
.B TESLAMATE_RS_PORT
Listen address and port.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_AUTH
Password backend,
.B local
or
.BR pam .
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_PAM_SERVICE
PAM service name. Default
.BR teslamate\-rs .
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_PAM_GROUP
Group a user must belong to in order to log in.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_PAM_ALLOW_ROOT
Permit root to log in. Refused by default.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_NO_LOGGER
Serve without starting the Owner API logger.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_POLL_SECS
Owner API poll interval in seconds.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_NO_INVOICES
.TQ
.B TESLAMATE_RS_INVOICE_SECS
Disable Supercharger invoice syncing, or set its interval in seconds.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_READ_POOL
Number of read-only SQLite connections.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_DEVICE_COUNTRY
Device country reported to the Tesla account API.
.TP
.B TESLAMATE_RS_WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN
.TQ
.B TESLAMATE_RS_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID
Public origin and relying-party ID for passkeys, for use behind a reverse
proxy. The Debian package is built without passkey support; see
.BR README.source .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/teslamate\-rs
Environment for the systemd service.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/teslamate\-rs
PAM configuration. Its presence selects the PAM backend by default.
.TP
.I /srv/teslamate\-rs/teslamate\-rs.sqlite
Database, with its WAL files alongside. Not removed when the package is.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, non-zero on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.PP
Packaging notes are in
.I /usr/share/doc/teslamate\-rs/README.Debian
and upstream documentation at
.UR https://github.com/teslamate\-org/teslamate
.UE .
